                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "A really short game, but to be expected from a story with only 60,000 words. However, this causes fast pacing and being thrown into the middle of the story with no real good explanation of things and makes it hard to get invested in. There are also way too many stats to keep track of for such a short game and it sometimes seems like stats get affected for no reason and that half of them don't even matter. I didn't even remember any of the characters names and eventually found myself bored and clicking ahead without bothering to read through half the options. There are a few different time skips and  its hard to keep track of things. I finished my first playthrough in maybe 25 minutes. Romance is almost nonexistent as you have one significant option [spoiler] (who you can't get a happy ending with because you're both loyal to your respective countries) [/spoiler] and 3 half-assed romances that don't even mean anything emotionally or game wise. Definitely not worth the 4 dollars when there are plenty of other longer and more engaging Choice of and Hosted games available.",
